WEBVTT

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:53.810
Once there was a dark night,

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:57.260
When we loved each other,

00:00:57.260 --> 00:01:02.060
So desperate, yet so sad,

00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:07.570
Never to return.

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:11.610
Lonely game, silly game,

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:15.180
There can be no retreat
from night and day!

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:16.780
Endless game,

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:21.530
Hold on tightly
to your broken dreams.

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:24.980
Follow me, stay with me,

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:28.380
Last chance,
time to risk it all!

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:32.420
It's so hard,

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:35.930
Baby, let me go.

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:37.970
Just Burning World!

00:01:56.980 --> 00:02:02.100
Crimson Media

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:45.830
It isn't safe to walk alone
in the city this late at night.

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:51.310
Besides, the stars warn
of great danger tonight.

00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:58.910
I'm with the Cyber Police.
Go back home where it's safe.

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:07.070
You can read all that from
the alignment of the stars?

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:09.190
Sometimes.

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:12.220
Perhaps I've misinterpreted
them tonight.

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:24.270
It's amazing that starlight
travels for thousands of years...

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:27.870
before finally reaching us.

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:34.750
But most starlight
is never even seen.

00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:37.950
It travels on through
the endless reaches of space.

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:40.350
It's a dark and lonely journey.

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:44.380
Eternal.

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:50.990
Not quite eternal.
It will finally end someday.

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:39.110
Help! I don't want to die!

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:55.000
The victim is
Ichiro Edajima, age 42.

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:57.270
Four prior arrests
for illegal research.

00:05:57.400 --> 00:06:03.480
Died at 12:25 AM, from blood loss
through the carotid artery.

00:06:03.480 --> 00:06:05.510
This is the third one.

00:06:06.320 --> 00:06:12.910
The same neck wound, blood loss,
and a password written in blood.

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:19.350
The news services are
reporting this as a "vampire killer."

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:25.780
If the case is not solved quickly,
it may lead to panic.

00:06:25.880 --> 00:06:27.830
So that's why they brought us in.

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:41.910
DNA? What kind of research
was he working on?

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:49.400
All of them were
unlicensed bio-engineers.

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:50.230
Ichiro Edajima
Sep. 1012:25 am

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:54.990
They were all known to work
for the black market.

00:06:55.400 --> 00:06:59.880
Find the link between them,
and you'll find the killer.

00:06:59.880 --> 00:07:03.420
Just solve it before we have
any more sensational murders.

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:08.630
Don't vampires sleep in the day?
We should wait until tonight.

00:07:08.720 --> 00:07:14.630
No, we need to find his coffin
and hammer a stake into his heart.

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:19.620
Whatever you like, so long
as you solve this case fast.

00:07:19.760 --> 00:07:23.870
varsus, have you figured out
those passwords yet?

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:26.870
No correlation found.

00:07:27.040 --> 00:07:30.740
It may be a manufacturing ID
or a registration number.

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:34.390
It "may be"?
What good does that do us, junkpile?

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:37.510
Let's trade varsus in
for some garlic and a cross.

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:41.590
This is your specialty.
Let me know what you find out.

00:07:42.280 --> 00:07:47.220
Wow, spooky case!
They got us looking for vampires now!

00:07:48.080 --> 00:07:52.150
Actually, the vampires of legend
were tragic creatures.

00:07:52.280 --> 00:07:55.670
Eternally young,
but forever craving human blood.

00:08:11.280 --> 00:08:14.550
I have no idea.

00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:22.310
I bought some drugs from him
five years ago, but that's all.

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:25.750
Hey, want a free sample?
It's legal.

00:08:25.880 --> 00:08:28.070
I guarantee:
Ten times in one night.

00:08:31.720 --> 00:08:34.150
I swear, I never met them!

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:40.230
I heard they got a big job from some vIP.
Maybe the syndicate.

00:08:41.240 --> 00:08:44.270
They specialized in DNA research.

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:50.310
I heard the syndicate hired them
to make an illegal proteroid.

00:08:50.440 --> 00:08:53.550
But somehow it doesn't sound
like a syndicate job.

00:08:53.680 --> 00:08:56.510
That's my gut feeling.

00:08:58.160 --> 00:09:02.550
The syndicate didn't kill them;
it was an amateur job.

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:07.660
They were worth lots more alive.

00:09:07.800 --> 00:09:12.630
So, can I show you a good time tonight?
I'll do you for free.

00:09:18.280 --> 00:09:21.820
Sorry we couldn't help you, Officer.

00:09:21.920 --> 00:09:27.830
By the way, some cyberpunks
heard you were in the area.

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:29.990
You'd better watch your step
out there.

00:09:42.160 --> 00:09:43.140
What do you want?

00:09:52.520 --> 00:09:56.030
A dog with a dog collar
belongs in a cage.

00:09:58.320 --> 00:10:02.870
And you belong on that dump,
since you're garbage.

00:10:04.360 --> 00:10:08.910
Hey, that's a good one!
I could bust a gut laughing!

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:10.630
Who put you up to this?

00:10:12.760 --> 00:10:18.270
Nobody! Lots of us like killing
dogs like you just for sport.

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:24.790
I suppose so. Besides,
who would rely on someone like you?

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:27.710
Go to hell!

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:33.750
Barbecue dog for dinner!

00:10:33.880 --> 00:10:37.660
Nah, his kind makes me sick.

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:50.030
- No! Ow!
- Hey.

00:10:51.760 --> 00:10:53.910
I'll let you off tonight
with just a minor penalty.

00:10:55.880 --> 00:10:57.830
Now get out of here
before you lose your heads.

00:11:02.840 --> 00:11:05.070
You still have the moves.

00:11:07.360 --> 00:11:11.270
It's been quite a while, Kelly.
When did you get back to Oedo?

00:11:12.200 --> 00:11:16.710
Stay out of this case.
I don't want to kill you.

00:11:16.840 --> 00:11:19.190
I don't want to fight you, either.

00:11:19.320 --> 00:11:20.540
Then...

00:11:21.160 --> 00:11:22.910
YOU stay out of this case.

00:11:25.720 --> 00:11:27.630
I still owe you.

00:11:27.720 --> 00:11:30.390
That was a long time ago.

00:11:30.520 --> 00:11:33.430
It was a nasty line of work.

00:11:33.920 --> 00:11:35.830
Yeah.

00:11:36.720 --> 00:11:41.150
Kelly, forget it.
You don't owe me anything.

00:12:16.800 --> 00:12:21.660
A Universal Access card
sends a valid ID to any computer.

00:12:22.640 --> 00:12:28.190
It's incredibly illegal.
Are you homesick for prison?

00:12:33.760 --> 00:12:35.550
What do you want to know?

00:12:36.200 --> 00:12:40.030
They had some new employer
for this job.

00:12:40.120 --> 00:12:47.700
But they never mentioned a name.
They were real cautious.

00:12:47.840 --> 00:12:53.430
Money was deposited directly
into their accounts each month.

00:12:53.800 --> 00:12:57.150
I didn't know criminals
kept bank accounts.

00:12:57.240 --> 00:13:02.230
The syndicate would have used cash;
this is too easy to trace.

00:13:02.440 --> 00:13:05.240
Yeah, their deposits
date back to July!

00:13:05.240 --> 00:13:08.030
They got 2,500,000 every month.

00:13:08.520 --> 00:13:12.030
The funds were transferred from...

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:15.000
Shuzo Saionji?

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:18.540
He's Honorary Chairman
of the Saionji Medical Foundation.

00:13:18.680 --> 00:13:21.310
Interesting. Thank you, Okyo.

00:13:30.360 --> 00:13:32.950
An honorary chairman who uses
unlicensed researchers.

00:13:49.520 --> 00:13:53.060
I did give them some help.

00:13:53.200 --> 00:13:58.030
Did you realize that they were
unlicensed criminals?

00:13:58.160 --> 00:14:01.070
Really? I didn't know.

00:14:01.200 --> 00:14:06.640
I just thought they were talented men
who fell on hard times.

00:14:06.640 --> 00:14:14.320
I wanted to help them out.
Call it an old man's whim.

00:14:14.600 --> 00:14:17.840
If your money funded
illegal research,

00:14:17.840 --> 00:14:20.220
you bear partial responsibility.

00:14:20.320 --> 00:14:24.470
That's only proper.
I'll be more careful in the future.

00:14:24.600 --> 00:14:26.630
Sir, you need to get some rest.

00:14:27.760 --> 00:14:30.670
Take care of your body, young man.

00:14:31.560 --> 00:14:36.270
If you want a long life,
get plenty of rest.

00:14:36.680 --> 00:14:39.750
I wish I could. Excuse me.

00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:44.640
Dr. Yamashita,
report to operating room six.

00:14:46.160 --> 00:14:47.710
Cryogenic Treatment Facility

00:14:51.160 --> 00:14:52.470
A capsule!

00:14:52.800 --> 00:14:55.750
It's the number
of a cold-sleep capsule!

00:15:07.400 --> 00:15:12.310
Use of the space elevator
is restricted.

00:15:12.480 --> 00:15:16.260
Insert proper ID.

00:15:18.840 --> 00:15:20.110
It really works.

00:16:24.240 --> 00:16:28.510
Remi Masuda. Admitted in 2504.

00:16:59.520 --> 00:17:02.190
Nothing here but rose petals.

00:17:48.200 --> 00:17:53.030
Use of the space elevator
is restricted.

00:17:53.440 --> 00:17:55.230
Insert proper ID.

00:18:35.160 --> 00:18:38.750
Another old man's whim?
The lying old coot.

00:18:41.360 --> 00:18:43.990
Centuries-old data?

00:18:44.920 --> 00:18:48.830
Yes. Look up a woman
named Remi Masuda.

00:18:49.320 --> 00:18:52.310
I don't know if they save data
for three centuries.

00:18:53.520 --> 00:18:58.030
Benten, I've started analyzing
that computer disk.

00:18:58.120 --> 00:18:58.990
What do you have?

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:02.150
It looks pretty bad.

00:19:02.880 --> 00:19:04.870
Get to the point.

00:19:05.240 --> 00:19:06.710
They created a new type of virus.

00:19:07.240 --> 00:19:10.350
It alters human cells,
granting unlimited cellular reproduction.

00:19:10.520 --> 00:19:13.550
It's an immortality virus.

00:19:13.720 --> 00:19:16.150
Nobel Prize material.

00:19:16.520 --> 00:19:17.710
That's not all.

00:19:18.160 --> 00:19:20.760
The virus stimulates
areas of the brain,

00:19:20.760 --> 00:19:22.670
giving a huge boost
to psychic abilities.

00:19:23.160 --> 00:19:25.320
Letting someone jump
into an upper-floor window...

00:19:25.320 --> 00:19:28.430
and snap a man's arm off?

00:19:28.760 --> 00:19:29.630
Yes.

00:19:29.960 --> 00:19:35.630
But the virus has one big flaw.
It halts blood production.

00:19:36.000 --> 00:19:40.710
Anyone infected would need
a perpetual supply of living blood.

00:19:41.120 --> 00:19:44.950
I see. That explains our vampire.

00:19:45.520 --> 00:19:49.710
Exactly. But there's still
one part I don't understand:

00:19:49.920 --> 00:19:53.620
What were the victims working on
when they were killed?

00:19:53.760 --> 00:19:56.110
Research on a second monster?

00:19:56.280 --> 00:20:01.590
I don't know.
It will take a while to figure this out.

00:20:02.000 --> 00:20:04.790
Let me know, once you find out.

00:20:16.240 --> 00:20:18.310
I'll give you a fighting chance.

00:20:18.440 --> 00:20:21.590
Killing has become
too easy for you.

00:20:22.080 --> 00:20:25.590
It's my job.
Don't worry about it.

00:20:26.360 --> 00:20:28.110
Who's your client?

00:20:29.800 --> 00:20:34.430
Let me guess: An old geezer
who should have died years ago.

00:20:35.440 --> 00:20:36.500
Do I win a cigar?

00:20:37.560 --> 00:20:38.910
Let's do it.

00:20:53.640 --> 00:20:56.830
What a wretched fate,
to come up against you.

00:20:58.040 --> 00:21:01.070
The stars are probably
in a bad alignment.

00:21:01.200 --> 00:21:02.310
Yes.

00:21:26.160 --> 00:21:27.750
You always were a good shot.

00:21:29.080 --> 00:21:32.990
Your job would have been easy,
but you thought you owed me.

00:21:34.160 --> 00:21:36.460
I agree.

00:21:45.600 --> 00:21:50.870
Shuzo Saionji, I'll peel your skin off
and make you suffer.

00:21:53.040 --> 00:21:57.550
Benten, I found your ancient data!
Can you hear me?

00:21:57.640 --> 00:21:58.800
Send it over.

00:21:58.800 --> 00:22:00.270
Roger.

00:22:02.760 --> 00:22:03.920
Identity check

00:22:03.920 --> 00:22:05.430
Identity check
Remi Masuda

00:22:10.520 --> 00:22:13.320
Hereditary anemia

00:22:13.320 --> 00:22:16.840
2504: Admitted to cryogenic facilities

00:22:16.840 --> 00:22:20.230
June 10, 2808: Pronounced dead

00:22:38.280 --> 00:22:42.150
Package for Mr. Kurozaki!
I need your signature.

00:22:45.760 --> 00:22:47.470
Damn, I'm too late!

00:22:54.240 --> 00:22:57.670
Monster!
You won't get away from me!

00:22:59.440 --> 00:23:03.830
That homing device will tell me
exactly where you're going.

00:23:10.280 --> 00:23:14.470
Right! Of course!
That explains it!

00:23:14.600 --> 00:23:18.470
Then I guess it's up to me
to finish your research.

00:23:30.200 --> 00:23:33.710
There were beautiful homes here
300 years ago.

00:23:34.920 --> 00:23:39.940
Back when you lived here,

00:23:40.840 --> 00:23:43.470
Remi Masuda.

00:23:55.400 --> 00:24:00.150
There was a beautiful rose garden
across the street.

00:24:00.280 --> 00:24:04.510
I sat on our terrace,
sipped tea, and looked at it.

00:24:05.360 --> 00:24:07.070
You must like roses.

00:24:07.360 --> 00:24:11.790
Your cold-sleep capsule
was filled with rose petals.

00:24:13.080 --> 00:24:16.390
My parents put them in there for me.

00:24:18.680 --> 00:24:20.960
I was born from an artificial womb,
but it malfunctioned.

00:24:20.960 --> 00:24:26.440
The cells in my body aged too quickly.
Nothing could be done.

00:24:26.440 --> 00:24:28.870
So I went into cold sleep
to wait for a cure.

00:24:29.880 --> 00:24:32.910
And while I slept, I dreamed.

00:24:33.040 --> 00:24:37.190
I dreamed of my happy life
here in this house.

00:24:37.320 --> 00:24:42.550
But then I woke from my sleep
and my nightmare began.

00:24:43.440 --> 00:24:46.590
I promise to end your
bad dream very soon.

00:25:01.560 --> 00:25:05.910
Benten, get away from that woman!
She's dangerous!

00:25:06.000 --> 00:25:08.990
I prefer dangerous women.

00:25:09.120 --> 00:25:13.110
Be serious!
Are you falling in love with a monster?

00:25:21.680 --> 00:25:25.750
Warning:
Cease hostilities immediately.

00:25:30.840 --> 00:25:32.030
You bastard!

00:25:39.240 --> 00:25:41.480
It's Hasegawa.
Execute the criminal.

00:25:41.480 --> 00:25:44.830
If Benten gets in your way,
kill him too.

00:25:46.280 --> 00:25:49.200
Damn junkpile! You ratted on him!

00:25:49.200 --> 00:25:50.030
Still...

00:25:50.360 --> 00:25:55.590
You can handle Benten.
You can just blow his head off.

00:25:56.040 --> 00:25:59.870
I'll do that, if the criminal is still alive
an hour from now.

00:26:10.240 --> 00:26:12.510
You did it, Goggles!

00:26:12.600 --> 00:26:15.270
Have the chemistry lab
make this up immediately.

00:26:59.000 --> 00:27:02.950
The Medical Academy.
She's heading for the space elevator.

00:27:03.080 --> 00:27:05.790
Perfect.
They have a shuttle port on the roof.

00:27:11.880 --> 00:27:17.470
Use of the space elevator is restricted.
Insert proper ID.

00:27:23.480 --> 00:27:24.430
Don't!

00:27:25.800 --> 00:27:27.550
Don't do it, Remi!

00:27:28.640 --> 00:27:31.870
I wasn't the only guinea pig.

00:27:32.640 --> 00:27:36.180
The cold-sleep capsules
provided plenty of subjects.

00:27:36.280 --> 00:27:38.030
They all died in horrible agony.

00:27:38.600 --> 00:27:41.750
It's their hatred that drives me.

00:27:42.800 --> 00:27:46.870
Now there's only one target
left for my revenge:

00:27:47.000 --> 00:27:51.270
Shuzo Saionji,
a demon disguised as a man.

00:27:51.400 --> 00:27:52.790
Wait!

00:28:08.400 --> 00:28:10.700
Out of my way! I'm going!

00:28:12.080 --> 00:28:14.910
You'll have to get past me first!

00:28:15.280 --> 00:28:17.110
Sounds like fun.

00:28:33.240 --> 00:28:37.350
I'll kill you myself if you
let the vampire get away.

00:28:40.800 --> 00:28:43.070
One more thing:

00:28:43.200 --> 00:28:48.060
The researchers were desperately working
to save their own lives.

00:28:48.200 --> 00:28:50.720
They needed a cure for the virus.

00:28:50.720 --> 00:28:53.320
I loaded the serum into this baton.

00:28:53.320 --> 00:28:55.990
Drive it into the vampire's heart.

00:29:16.440 --> 00:29:19.190
I've been waiting for you, Remi.

00:29:19.880 --> 00:29:22.440
Demon! Why did you do this?

00:29:22.560 --> 00:29:25.020
Nothing is more terrifying
than death.

00:29:25.480 --> 00:29:29.070
I have always dreamed
of immortality.

00:29:29.160 --> 00:29:33.430
But I never wanted immortality.

00:29:33.560 --> 00:29:38.870
I chose cold sleep in the hope
that someday I could be cured.

00:29:39.600 --> 00:29:41.670
I didn't have much time.

00:29:41.760 --> 00:29:46.390
I needed to achieve immortality
before this body failed me.

00:29:47.080 --> 00:29:52.830
And thanks to you,
the experiment was a success.

00:30:05.560 --> 00:30:08.230
The experiment was a success.

00:30:15.200 --> 00:30:22.030
Not only am I immortal,
but I've also gained incredible power!

00:30:28.400 --> 00:30:33.260
As thanks, I will grant you death.

00:30:34.400 --> 00:30:40.990
I will feed on the blood
that flows in your immortal veins.

00:31:13.600 --> 00:31:15.790
Release Remi Masuda!

00:31:16.240 --> 00:31:18.800
So, you're still alive.

00:31:19.040 --> 00:31:23.750
The Honorary Chairman
of the Saionji Medical Foundation.

00:31:24.200 --> 00:31:25.840
That's quite a title.

00:31:25.840 --> 00:31:31.710
But you don't have the right
to use your patients as guinea pigs.

00:31:33.320 --> 00:31:36.670
Look at what I've accomplished.

00:31:39.800 --> 00:31:42.390
No one can kill me now!

00:31:47.800 --> 00:31:49.910
You know too much.

00:32:20.120 --> 00:32:24.790
You might as well give up.
There's nowhere you can run.

00:33:19.280 --> 00:33:21.550
Where are you hiding?

00:33:23.800 --> 00:33:25.710
Right here, Saionji!

00:34:38.600 --> 00:34:43.590
I told you, no one can kill me.

00:34:44.440 --> 00:34:47.150
I will live forever.

00:34:47.760 --> 00:34:51.630
Forever? That's absurd.

00:34:51.880 --> 00:34:56.880
Everything in this universe
has both a beginning and an end.

00:34:56.880 --> 00:35:03.110
Nothing lasts forever,
except for one thing:

00:35:05.720 --> 00:35:08.510
Your crimes are eternal.

00:36:06.960 --> 00:36:11.630
Please, let me die, too.

00:36:26.120 --> 00:36:30.390
It's finally over.
My nightmare has ended.

00:36:31.080 --> 00:36:35.030
Yes. From now on,
you'll only have good dreams.

00:36:37.960 --> 00:36:40.550
Yes, I will.

00:37:01.360 --> 00:37:03.230
Goodbye.

00:37:42.640 --> 00:37:47.640
It's amazing that starlight travels
for thousands of years...

00:37:47.640 --> 00:37:51.070
before finally reaching us.

00:37:51.920 --> 00:37:55.670
But most starlight
is never even seen.

00:37:56.200 --> 00:37:58.580
It travels on through
the endless reaches of space.

00:37:58.920 --> 00:38:01.110
It's a dark and lonely journey.

00:38:01.360 --> 00:38:03.230
Eternal.

00:38:06.640 --> 00:38:10.260
Now, nothing will disturb
your sleep ever again.

00:38:10.560 --> 00:38:14.750
You will travel forever,
alongside the starlight.

00:39:25.400 --> 00:39:31.360
I just want to say I love you

00:39:31.360 --> 00:39:37.350
Ever so gently I whisper.

00:39:39.600 --> 00:39:45.150
Before time moves on without us

00:39:45.240 --> 00:39:50.310
And takes you away forever

00:39:50.680 --> 00:39:56.070
I just want to say I love you

00:39:56.160 --> 00:40:01.310
Ever so gently I whisper.

00:40:01.960 --> 00:40:07.350
Putting my trust and faith in you

00:40:07.480 --> 00:40:12.340
I will open my heart to you

00:40:13.000 --> 00:40:18.270
I always want to be able...

00:40:18.640 --> 00:40:23.500
to continue my search for you.
